      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": "### Study: Seven Hours of Sleep Ideal in Middle to Old Age\nSeven hours may be the ideal amount of time for people in middle and old age to sleep, new research suggests.\nIn a study from the University of Cambridge and China’s Fudan University, "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q21",
        "placeholder": "21"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " 500,000 British adults between the ages of 38 and 73 completed surveys about their sleep. Many scientists also "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q22",
        "placeholder": "22"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " cognitive（认知的）tests, and about a third completed survey on their mental "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q23",
        "placeholder": "23"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " and well-being.\nThe results "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q24",
        "placeholder": "24"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " that participants who said they slept an "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q25",
        "placeholder": "25"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " of about seven hours a day did best in the cognitive tests, had the lowest symptoms（症状）of anxiety and depression, and had the highest feelings of well-being. Even those who slept more than seven hours did not do as well as those who slept seven. “For every hour that you moved away from seven hours you got worse,” co-author Barbara Sahakian told The Guardian.\nBrain scans done on almost 40,000 participants showed that the areas of the brain most affected by sleep included the memory center. However, Sahakian said the researchers are not yet sure why too much sleep could have a "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q26",
        "placeholder": "26"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " effect, although one idea was that people might\n"
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q27",
        "placeholder": "27"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " longer time in bed if they sleep poorly and wake up a lot.\nHowever, Russell Foster, a sleep expert at the University of Oxford who did not take "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q28",
        "placeholder": "28"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " in the study, disagreed with the results, telling CNN that the ideal amount of sleep is different for everyone, and that “one size does not fit all.”\nSahakian said that "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q29",
        "placeholder": "29"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " a good night’s sleep is important for people of all ages, adding, “I think it is as important as getting "
       },
       {
        "type": "blank",
        "key": "q30",
        "placeholder": "30"
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": " .”"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
